>> title: Hong Kong Egg Sandwich
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: eggs, sandwich, bread, hong kong, breakfast, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: daan ji, 蛋治, egg sandwich, HK egg sandwich, scrambled egg sandwich, soft egg sandwich
>> servings: 1
>> time: 10 min
>> slack: narrow — the egg comes out of the pan while it still looks underdone and sets on the way to the bread; cooked until it looks right it goes to curds and will not hold as a sheet

>> step: beat it smooth, no streaks
Beat @eggs{3%large} with @evaporated milk{1%Tbs}, @fine salt{1/4%tsp} and @white pepper{1/8%tsp} until there are no streaks left.

>> step: fold 3 min on the lowest heat, off wet
Cook @&(~1)egg{} in @unsalted butter{2%tsp} in a #nonstick pan{} on the lowest heat the burner will hold for ~fold{3%min}, dragging it in slow folds and taking it off while it is still wet.

>> step: butter both faces to the edge
Spread @salted butter{2%tsp}(softened) over both faces of @white sandwich bread{2%slices} right to the edges.

>> step: fold it in, crusts off, cut in triangles
Fold @&(~2)soft egg{} into @&(~1)buttered bread{} as one sheet rather than a spoonful, cut the crusts off all four sides, and cut it corner to corner into triangles.
